  "historical_unknowns": [
    "These are constructed LLVM IR inputs, with no C preprocessing stage or recovered application failure.",
    "The crash is confirmed; root cause and target constraint/type support need investigation before selecting a repair."
  ],
  "resolution": {
    "change": "patches/llvm-mos/0058-aarch64-inline-asm-unknown-type.patch",
    "causal_explanation": "Non-simple operand types map to MVT::Other in ParseConstraints. AArch64 r/x handlers queried its undefined bit size; both now return no register class before that query. Existing SelectionDAG diagnostics reject the operand cleanly. The guard-only link repairs the original input with the original SelectionDAG object, while the 0057 baseline still aborts without the guard.",
    "trigger_check": "The unchanged original load i4096 and r inline-asm call are passed directly to llc with the recorded AArch64/O0/SelectionDAG/verifier/finalize-isel settings. The runner requires compiler exit 1 and exactly the allocation diagnostic, rejecting aborts and other errors.",
    "regression": {
      "path": "docs/defects/evidence/2026-09-25-selectiondag-inlineasm/integer-many-virtual.ll",
      "sha256": "530467a0e45905dc3c9ab9a0b31bebc8630e8825dd89f12a45f7ebda4edea39d"
    },
    "candidate": {
      "command": "python3 dev/check-aarch64-asm-type-diagnostic.py --llc /home/will/llvm-mos-65816/build/aarch64-asm-type-fix/llc",
      "working_directory": "/home/will/llvm-mos-65816",
